Third-Party Attributions

This software incorporates third-party packages from its dependency tree. The
complete inventory — every package, version, and SPDX license identifier — is
generated by `bun run licenses` and committed to THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md at the
repository root. Regenerate that file after any dependency change.

License distribution across 860 unique third-party packages:

    749  MIT
     42  Apache-2.0
     33  ISC
     22  BSD-2-Clause / BSD-3-Clause
      4  MPL-2.0
      2  LGPL-3.0-or-later
      7  other permissive (0BSD, CC0-1.0, CC-BY-4.0, Unlicense, and
           dual-license expressions including MIT/WTFPL, MIT/CC0-1.0,
           AFL-2.1/BSD-3-Clause, BSD-2-Clause/MIT/Apache-2.0)

No packages declare a GPL, AGPL, or SSPL license. The following copyleft-
licensed packages are present:

  - MPL-2.0: axe-core, lightningcss (both reached only through development /
    build tooling — eslint-config-next and @tailwindcss/postcss respectively —
    and are not part of the distributed runtime).

  - LGPL-3.0-or-later: @img/sharp-libvips-linux-x64 and
    @img/sharp-libvips-linuxmusl-x64 — native libvips binaries reached as an
    optional dependency of Next.js (sharp), used for image optimization. They
    are dynamically loaded, unmodified, and installed from the public npm
    registry. As LGPL components, attribution is recorded here; their license
    texts are reproduced with the packages as distributed by their authors.
